      "about": "Microsoft Certified Azure Data & AI Engineering Professional | AI & ML Enthusiast\n\nChanakya is a 10X+ Microsoft Certified Data & AI Engineer with nearly 7 years of experience in designing, building, and optimizing cloud-based data engineering solutions on Microsoft Azure. \nHe has strong expertise across the end-to-end data lifecycle—from extracting data from diverse source systems to orchestrating pipelines and transforming data into analytics-ready datasets aligned with complex business requirements.\n\nCurrently, he is working at Wipro as a Senior Data Engineer, supporting large-scale enterprise data platforms for a US-based Telecom client. His responsibilities include data orchestration, pipeline optimization, performance tuning, and reliable data transformations, while collaborating closely with solution architects and data engineering leads to deliver scalable and resilient data solutions.\n\nPreviously at IQVIA, Chanakya contributed to multiple enterprise-grade data initiatives, working as a SME cum architect for various Data transformation projects which led to business growth in the IQVIA DIA Tech team. He had implemented Medallion-based data processing patterns and standardized data engineering frameworks. His core Azure technology stack includes Azure Databricks, Azure Data Factory, Azure Storage (ADLS Gen2, Blob), Azure Synapse Analytics, Azure DevOps (CI/CD)Microsoft Fabric, and other Azure services.\n\nPrior to this, he worked at Cognizant as an Azure Data Engineer, delivering data solutions across Media & Communications, Retail, Healthcare, and Banking Financial Services domains, with strong exposure to Big Data ecosystems such as Hadoop and Apache Spark. His technical strengths are complemented by proficiency in Python, SQL, and Core Java, enabling him to build robust, scalable, and maintainable data pipelines.\n\nDeeply enthusiastic about Data, Cloud, and AI, Chanakya actively explores how these technologies are reshaping modern data platforms.\n\n“Learning has to be learned in the best possible manner—everything else follows.”",
